## Maximum Product Subarray

## Problem Statement

Given an integer array nums, find a subarray that has the largest product, and return the product.

The test cases are generated so that the answer will fit in a 32-bit integer.

Note that the product of an array with a single element is the value of that element.

 ##Example 

Example 1:
Input: nums = [2,3,-2,4]
Output: 6
Explanation: [2,3] has the largest product 6.

Example 2:
Input: nums = [-2,0,-1]
Output: 0
Explanation: The result cannot be 2, because [-2,-1] is not a subarray.

## Approach - Brute Force 
Use an outer loop to select every possible starting index i.
For each starting index, initialize prod = 1.
Use an inner loop to extend the subarray from index i to the right.
At every step, multiply the current element with prod.
After calculating the product of each subarray, update maxProd with the maximum value found so far.
Finally, return maxProd.


## Code -

class Solution {
    public int maxProduct(int[] nums) {
        int maxProd = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

        for(int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++){
            int prod = 1;
            for(int j = i; j < nums.length; j++){
                prod = prod * nums[j];
                maxProd = Math.max(maxProd,prod);
            }
        }
        return maxProd;
    }
}

## Complexity - 
O(n) - tc
O(1) - sc

